From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:59:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rust: drm: gpuvm: lock a shared reservation once in
 exec_lock

GpuVm::exec_lock() runs drm_gpuvm_exec_lock() with flags 0, so it
locks the VM reservation and then every external object. Two GEM
objects can share one reservation: a client that closes its handle to an
imported dma-buf and imports the same dma-buf again gets a second GEM
object for it, while the first one keeps its GPUVAs until the VM's
in-flight jobs retire (handle-close cleanup is deferred in
Vm::drop_mappings()). drm_exec_lock_obj() then takes the shared
dma_resv a second time with the same ticket, ww_mutex returns -EALREADY,
and without DRM_EXEC_IGNORE_DUPLICATES drm_exec passes it up.

On G16 every SUBMIT reads its control streams through Vm::read_user(),
which takes this lock, and the stream gate turns any read_user() error
into EFAULT. mpv with zero-copy VA-API into its Vulkan output re-imports
the decoder surface each frame, so on the J604 a 1080p video got a blank
window, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST and "IOCTL: submit failed! (... err:
EFAULT)" on its first frame after a seek. The idle-VM restore path takes
the same lock and had the same exposure.

Set DRM_EXEC_IGNORE_DUPLICATES, as the C users of drm_gpuvm_exec and
drm_exec do for the same reason (nouveau_sched.c, panthor, xe, msm,
imagination): a shared reservation is locked and unlocked once, and
nothing else changes. exec_lock_vm() shares the initializer; its
VM-reservation-only lock is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 rust/kernel/drm/gpuvm/mod.rs | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/drm/gpuvm/mod.rs b/rust/kernel/drm/gpuvm/mod.rs
index 8b40308767..66adaf99e0 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/drm/gpuvm/mod.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/drm/gpuvm/mod.rs
@@ -335,11 +335,14 @@ impl<T: DriverGpuVm> GpuVm<T> {
         let mut vm_exec = KBox::init(
             init!(bindings::drm_gpuvm_exec {
                 vm: self.as_raw(),
-                flags: if interruptible {
-                    bindings::DRM_EXEC_INTERRUPTIBLE_WAIT
-                } else {
-                    0
-                },
+                // Two GEM objects can share one reservation (a dma-buf imported again while
+                // the closed object still has mappings); lock it once, as C drm_exec users do.
+                flags: bindings::DRM_EXEC_IGNORE_DUPLICATES
+                    | if interruptible {
+                        bindings::DRM_EXEC_INTERRUPTIBLE_WAIT
+                    } else {
+                        0
+                    },
                 exec: Default::default(),
                 extra: match (is_ext, obj) {
                     (true, Some(obj)) => bindings::drm_gpuvm_exec__bindgen_ty_1 {
